{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PartitionListBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.normalizedSum_iff_molien","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.normalizedSum_iff_molien","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.lean#L181-L190","doc":"**Non-vacuity / consistency check at `n = 2`.** The general `molienSum` at `n = 2` is *literally*\nthe concrete left-hand side proved in `MolienFakeDegree.molien_qanalogue_n2` once the two-element\n`Nat.Partition 2` index is enumerated — so the general statement is a faithful lift, not a new (and\npossibly weaker) object. Recorded as the seam a future faithfulness bridge closes; see the module\ndocstring. The equivalence `molienSum_eq_qFactorial_iff` therefore says, at `n = 2`, exactly that\n`normalizedSum 2 q = 1`, the `n = 2` instance of the mathematical content now closed in\n`NormalizedSumUnconditional`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.molienSum_eq_qFactorial_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.molienSum_eq_qFactorial_iff","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.lean#L163-L179","doc":"**The reduction, as an equivalence.** For `1 < q` (so `[n]_q! ≠ 0`),\n\n  `molienSum n q = qFactorial q n  ⟺  normalizedSum n q = 1`.\n\nThe forward direction cancels the nonzero `[n]_q!`; the reverse multiplies it back. This isolates\nthe genuine mathematical content — `normalizedSum n q = 1` — from the bookkeeping. That content\n(bean `qou-3quc`) is closed in `NormalizedSumUnconditional`, so this equivalence now *delivers*\n`molienSum n q = [n]_q!` (`NormalizedSumUnconditional.molienSum_eq_qFactorial`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.molienSum_eq_qFactorial_mul_normalized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.molienSum_eq_qFactorial_mul_normalized","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.lean#L145-L161","doc":"**General-`n` factoring.** Every summand's `qDim` carries the same numerator `[n]_q!` — because\n`(toList p).sum = n` for every `p ⊢ n` — so it factors out of the whole sum:\n\n  `molienSum n q = [n]_q! · normalizedSum n q`.\n\nSorry-free, general `n`. The one non-formal ingredient is\n`PartitionListBridge.toList_sum : (toList p).sum = n`, which is precisely the statement that the\n`Nat.Partition n` index keeps the size fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.normalizedSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.normalizedSum","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.lean#L137-L143","doc":"**The normalised hook sum** `Σ_{p ⊢ n} f_p · q^{−κ_p} / ∏_x [h_x]_q`. The identity\n`molienSum n q = [n]_q!` is equivalent to `normalizedSum n q = 1` (see\n`molienSum_eq_qFactorial_iff`); `normalizedSum n q = 1` for general `n` is the mathematical content\n(bean `qou-3quc`), now proved in `NormalizedSumUnconditional.normalizedSum_eq_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.molienSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.molienSum","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.lean#L125-L135","doc":"**The general-`n` Molien / fake-degree sum**, indexed by the canonical partition Fintype\n`Nat.Partition n` (the same index as `QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideHolds`).\n\n  `molienSum n q = Σ_{p ⊢ n} f_p · q^{−κ_p} · qDim q λ_p`\n\nwith `f_p = dimSYT p` (the genuine `#SYT`), `κ_p = contentSum λ_p`, and `λ_p = toList p` the parts\nsorted weakly decreasing. For `n = 2, 3, 4` its value is `qFactorial q n` by\n`MolienFakeDegree.molien_qanalogue_n{2,3,4}` (the concrete, per-partition proofs). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.qDim_eq_qFactorial_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.qDim_eq_qFactorial_div","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.lean#L117-L121","doc":"**`qDim q λ = [|λ|]_q! / ∏_x [h_x]_q`, definitionally.** `qDim` is *defined* as the q-factorial of\nthe size over this very hook product, so the split holds by `rfl`. This is the structural fact the\nreduction below turns on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.hookProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.hookProd","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MolienFakeDegreeGeneralN.lean#L105-L115","doc":"The **hook-length product** `∏_{x ∈ λ} [h_x]_q`, i.e. the denominator of `qDim`.\n\nThis is the exact `foldl` appearing in `QPartitionCombinatorics.qDim`, named so the\nnumerator/denominator split can be reasoned about. Generic `[Field R]` (§7c). ","signatureChunk":0}]}